<title>BELGIUM: EU increases raw sugar import forecast.</title>
<headline>EU increases raw sugar import forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The early forecast for special preferential imports of raw cane sugar from ACP countries to the European Union was put at 300,000 tonnes for 1997/98 on Wednesday compared with 296,000 tonnes last year, a Commission official said.</p>
<p>The EU sugar management committee based their increased forecast on production figures from the French overseas territories but no figures are yet available for the French Antilles, the official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This was a very early forecast in advance of the first raw sugar balance sheet due to be fixed in June with the final sheet being fixed in February,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
